{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1017507-another-reason-to-take-spirit-more-access-to-quintessence","id":1017507,"title":"Another reason to take Spirit: more access to Quintessence.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-14T22:55:34-08:00","id":1017507,"title":"Another reason to take Spirit: more access to Quintessence.","content":"Spirits aren't Quintessence batteries, obviously. But kind of like even though you don't hang out with a certain crowd <i>just</i> because they have drugs, it is a benefit. The most reliable way to hang out with spirits is to have Spirit.<br /> <br /> Obviously this isn't news to many people here, but I think it's something people forget about which is one of the reasons Spirit tends to get overlooked. Spirit is a more versatile than a Node background and doesn't rely on you staying in one location.* The biggest downside is that you also need Prime 3, so it wouldn't be for everyone. Just another option.<br /> <br /> *Although see my alternate Background, &quot;Conduit&quot;: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/948419-revision-of-node-background-that-allows-free-ranging-quintessence-gain\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ntessence-gain</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T08:52:57-08:00","id":1017672,"title":"","content":"I agree. I've thought about this as well. Depending on how important Quint ends up being (scarcity, whether the benefits are worth it, etc.), it seems like munching down spirits to digest their Gnosis to get lovely, lovely Quint might be VERY important.<br /> <br /> It does sort of change the image one has of the VE's to have them killing BEM then taking them back to the engine room to toss the body into some gadget to render it down to power the ship.... And, geeze, is it possible to use EDE &quot;juice&quot; to stave off Void Adaptation? (&quot;No, I don't know what happened to the thing we killed yesterday that looked like Giger's wet dream... Just take your pills...&quot;) Seems counterintuitive and I don't want to go book-diving to see if there's anything relevant out there. But, still... might that work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T13:02:03-08:00","id":1017766,"title":"","content":"Just don't forget that you're likely going to become infamous in spirit circles. I believe that something like this came up in the Dreamspeaker Tradition book, and it made sure to warn that using Spirit to dominate and control, not to mention devouring, spirits might end up making things difficult for you later. Reputation is a real concern when it comes to spirit dealings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T15:43:04-08:00","id":1017828,"title":"","content":"That might matter to Dreamspeakers, but that doesn't mean it matters as much to many other kinds of mages. I can see Wu Lung eating spirits with ceremony and delectation, so long as it is done appropriately. Hermetics would probably find some multi-step alchemical process to remove the &quot;devouring&quot; aspect, but, particularly for some Houses, I doubt they give a fig if the spirits get pissed about it. After all, that's what having greater WILL is all about. VEs certainly aren't going to care what EDE's think, if they even CAN do such a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T18:01:57-08:00","id":1017882,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking more along the lines of The Spirit Kiss (2E p. 218) where they're giving you Quintessence willingly, probably in exchange for some favor. It actually says it only requires Prime 2, along with Spirit 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T19:14:18-08:00","id":1017910,"title":"","content":"Indeed, it's fully possible to gain Quintessence from the Umbra without destroying any spirits. Doing trades is better in the long run, since it gives you a reputation as a useful mortal to know, rather than as a parasite that drains innocent Umbrood.<br /> <br /> You could also use Spirit 3 to travel the Umbra and harvest Tass or free flowing Quintessence. The material world is notable for being scarce in such things (save for Nodes and Junctures), so it stands to reason that the Umbra will have it in greater abundance. You become a sort of gatherer, scouring Umbral plains for flowers fed by moonlight, or potent mushrooms on the undersides of towering trees, or mineral deposits in a stygian cave.<br /> <br /> Since it's in the form of exotic Tass, it can be brought back to the material world and traded with other Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T19:53:29-08:00","id":1017923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1017507-another-reason-to-take-spirit-more-access-to-quintessence?p=1017910#post1017910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, it's fully possible to gain Quintessence from the Umbra without destroying any spirits. Doing trades is better in the long run, since it gives you a reputation as a useful mortal to know, rather than as a parasite that drains innocent Umbrood.<br /> <br /> You could also use Spirit 3 to travel the Umbra and harvest Tass or free flowing Quintessence. The material world is notable for being scarce in such things (save for Nodes and Junctures), so it stands to reason that the Umbra will have it in greater abundance. You become a sort of gatherer, scouring Umbral plains for flowers fed by moonlight, or potent mushrooms on the undersides of towering trees, or mineral deposits in a stygian cave.<br /> <br /> Since it's in the form of exotic Tass, it can be brought back to the material world and traded with other Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure such a tass would retain its potency if it were to cross the gauntlet. The sudden exposure to sleeper consensus may cause it to wilt, especially in areas where the gauntlet is weak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T20:43:01-08:00","id":1017932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1017507-another-reason-to-take-spirit-more-access-to-quintessence?p=1017923#post1017923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure such a tass would retain its potency if it were to cross the gauntlet. The sudden exposure to sleeper consensus may cause it to wilt, especially in areas where the gauntlet is weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Tass is Tass. You don't see Tass collected from the material side of the Gauntlet losing its potency when people are around. If Disbelief is the problem, hide the Tass in a container so no one can see it. Not that all Umbral Tass would be subject to Disbelief on sight anyway. A blue mushroom or a handful of mineral powder isn't going to look unnatural to most people. Unlike a Bygone, an inanimate object with weird properties could be a prop, or the results of some weird cultivation or manufacturing.<br /> <br /> Also, why would a place with a weaker Gauntlet be <i>more</i> hostile to Umbral Tass? With the sole exception of Technocracy labs (and then only with Dimensional Science), the Gauntlet gets thinner the farther you are from civilization. The Consensus has less power there. If anything, Umbral Tass should hold up <i>better</i> in places with weak Gauntlets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T21:26:40-08:00","id":1017942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1017507-another-reason-to-take-spirit-more-access-to-quintessence?p=1017932#post1017932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? Tass is Tass. You don't see Tass collected from the material side of the Gauntlet losing its potency when people are around. If Disbelief is the problem, hide the Tass in a container so no one can see it. Not that all Umbral Tass would be subject to Disbelief on sight anyway. A blue mushroom or a handful of mineral powder isn't going to look unnatural to most people. Unlike a Bygone, an inanimate object with weird properties could be a prop, or the results of some weird cultivation or manufacturing.<br /> <br /> Also, why would a place with a weaker Gauntlet be <i>more</i> hostile to Umbral Tass? With the sole exception of Technocracy labs (and then only with Dimensional Science), the Gauntlet gets thinner the farther you are from civilization. The Consensus has less power there. If anything, Umbral Tass should hold up <i>better</i> in places with weak Gauntlets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, meant to say &quot;where the gauntlet is strong&quot;. Sorry about that.<br /> <br /> Tass always loses potency over time. It's the whole &quot;Ice melts to water&quot; analogy.<br /> The way I imagine umbral Tass is Tass which is partially made of spirit, so as the spirit side of it is removed, its stability falters.<br /> <br /> It's the same reason why Vampires have a hard time in the spirit world because &quot;real&quot; blood is difficult to come by. Anything that resembles blood is actual some kind of spiritual ectoplasm, and may not have the same effect for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 12-16-2016, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T21:49:02-08:00","id":1017951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1017507-another-reason-to-take-spirit-more-access-to-quintessence?p=1017942#post1017942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, meant to say &quot;where the gauntlet is strong&quot;. Sorry about that.<br /> <br /> Tass always loses potency over time. It's the whole &quot;Ice melts to water&quot; analogy.<br /> The way I imagine umbral Tass is Tass which is partially made of spirit, so as the spirit side of it is removed, it's stability falters.<br /> <br /> It's the same reason why Vampires have a hard time in the spirit world because &quot;real&quot; blood is difficult to come by. Anything that resembles blood is actual some kind of spiritual ectoplasm, and may not have the same effect for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe if the Mage also had Matter 3, they could convert it to material Tass of equal value. If the character doesn't have that knowledge, there's probably Mages who make part of their living performing that service in exchange for a cut of the profits.<br /> <br /> Now I'm imagining a Chantry that doubles as an Umbral trading post, complete with a Node (that keeps the Gauntlet thin and easy to cross through), storage space warded for safety and increased shelf life, and gates allowing Mages to teleport in from other Chantries or individual Sancta.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}